iate"><addressbook><last-name>ABE, NAOTO</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>HASEGAWA, MITSUTOSHI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>MITSUTAKE, HIDEAKI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>MIYAZAKI, TOSHIHIKO</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>ONO, TAKEO</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>TODOKORO, YASUYUKI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>YAMADA, SHUJI</last-name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><last-name>YAMAGUCHI, EIJI</last-name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>An electron beam display comprising a first substrate (1011) having an electron emitting device (1012); a second substrate having a transparent substrate (1017), a phosphor layer (1018) provided on the transparent substrate, a mask member for demarcating the phosphor layer into light-emitting regions, an accelerating electrode (1019) for accelerating electrons emitted from the electron emitting device, and an antistatic film (1022); a vacuum enclosure constituted of a member including the first and second substrates spaced from each other and having therein a spacer member (1020) for maintaining the spacing and a getter; and a drive circuit including a scanning line drive circuit for sequentially applying a scanning signal to scanning lines (1014) and a control line drive circuit for applying a modulation signal corresponding to image information to all the control lines (1013) at once synchronously with the scanning lines.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention se rapporte à un afficheur à faisceau électronique comportant un premier substrat (1011) ayant un dispositif émetteur d'électrons (1012); un second substrat ayant un substrat transparent (1017), une couche fluorescente (1018) disposée sur le substrat transparent, un élément masque permettant de séparer la couche fluorescente en régions électroluminescentes, une électrode d'accélération (1019) conçue pour accélérer les électrons émis par le dispositif émetteur d'électrons et un film antistatique (1022); une enceinte sous vide constituée d'un élément comprenant les premier et second substrats espacés l'un de l'autre et comprenant un élément écarteur (1020) conçu pour maintenir l'écartement et un getter; et un circuit de commande des lignes de balayage conçu pour appliquer séquentiellement un signal de balayage à des lignes de balayage (1014) et un circuit d'attaque des lignes de commande conçu pour appliquer un signal de modulation correspondant aux informations d'images à toutes les lignes de commande (1013) en même temps, de manière synchrone aux lignes de balayage.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>